messages.content:
Review this proposed change (review round 1).

Repository: infra-eks at ref 382379b82b8dcb43a8c4c7f0a8372fe18c24fadb (use these as the repo and ref arguments of read_repo_file).

Hypothesis about the failure: The Terraform configuration in versions.tf specifies an invalid AWS provider version constraint (>= 99.0.0) that does not exist in the Terraform registry, causing terraform init to fail when querying available provider packages.

Proposed unified diff:
```diff
--- a/versions.tf
+++ b/versions.tf
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
   required_version = ">= 1.5.0"
   required_providers {
     aws = {
       source  = "hashicorp/aws"
-      version = ">= 99.0.0"
+      version = ">= 5.0.0"
     }
   }
 }
```

Current contents of versions.tf:
```
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.5.0"
  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source  = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = ">= 99.0.0"
    }
  }
}

```

